# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source documents are NOT committed. They are large (879 MB) and one exceeds
# GitHub's 100 MiB hard per-file limit (a second sits at 98 MiB). The repo
# commits *extracted data* plus a hash manifest so any figure can be
# re-verified against the original. See docs/PROVENANCE.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
sources/
build/

# Never commit source formats directly
*.pdf
*.xlsx
# ...except the generated exports (stages 101 and 103). `git add -A` silently
# skips an ignored file, so without these negations a workbook was
# committed-but-absent once: the README linked it, the tests passed against the
# local copy, and the URL 404'd. The tab map had been left off this list — it
# was tracked, so updates staged fine, but a delete-and-regenerate would have
# recreated the same silent 404.
!data/exports/MFAS_Data_Warehouse.xlsx
!data/exports/MFAS_Workbook_Tab_Map.xlsx
*.xls
*.docx
*.zip

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
